<div class="max-w-2xl p-4 m-auto space-y-4">
  <h1 class="text-xl font-black text-center mt-12">
    Registration funnel
  </h1>

  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead>
      <tr class="border-b text-left">
        <th class="py-2 pr-2">Step</th>
        <% @windows.each_key do |label| %>
          <th class="py-2 px-2 text-right"><%= label %></th>
        <% end %>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% Root::FunnelController::STEPS.each do |step| %>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 <%= 'font-bold' if step == 'password_created' %>">
          <td class="py-2 pr-2 font-mono"><%= step %></td>
          <% @windows.each_key do |label| %>
            <% count = @counts[label][step] || 0 %>
            <% started = @counts[label]['started'] || 0 %>
            <td class="py-2 px-2 text-right tabular-nums">
              <%= count %>
              <% if step != 'started' && started.positive? %>
                <span class="text-secondary text-xs">(<%= (100.0 * count / started).round %>%)</span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          <% end %>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
      <tr class="text-secondary">
        <td class="py-2 pr-2 font-mono">↳ of which resends</td>
        <% @windows.each_key do |label| %>
          <td class="py-2 px-2 text-right tabular-nums"><%= @resends[label] %></td>
        <% end %>
      </tr>
      <tr class="text-secondary">
        <td class="py-2 pr-2 font-mono">↳ bounced (notice shown)</td>
        <% @windows.each_key do |label| %>
          <% bounced = @bounces[label].values.sum %>
          <% sent = @counts[label]['mail_sent'] || 0 %>
          <td class="py-2 px-2 text-right tabular-nums align-top">
            <%= bounced %>
            <% if sent.positive? && bounced.positive? %>
              <span class="text-xs">(<%= (100.0 * bounced / sent).round %>% of sent)</span>
            <% end %>
            <% if bounced.positive? %>
              <div class="text-xs">
                <% @bounces[label].sort_by { |reason, n| [-n, reason] }.each do |reason, n| %>
                  <div><span class="font-mono"><%= reason %></span> <%= n %></div>
                <% end %>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </td>
        <% end %>
      </tr>
      <tr class="text-secondary" id="mail_failed">
        <td class="py-2 pr-2 font-mono">↳ mail failed (not sent)</td>
        <% @windows.each_key do |label| %>
          <% failed = @mail_failures[label].values.sum %>
          <td class="py-2 px-2 text-right tabular-nums align-top <%= 'text-red-600' if failed.positive? %>">
            <%= failed %>
            <div class="text-xs">
              <% @mail_failures[label].sort_by { |kind, n| [-n, kind] }.each do |kind, n| %>
                <div><span class="font-mono"><%= kind %></span> <%= n %></div>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          </td>
        <% end %>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 class="font-bold pt-4">By week</h2>

  <table class="w-full text-sm" id="weekly">
    <thead>
      <tr class="border-b text-left">
        <th class="py-2 pr-2">Week of</th>
        <th class="py-2 px-2 text-right">started</th>
        <th class="py-2 px-2 text-right">mail_sent</th>
        <th class="py-2 px-2 text-right">mail_failed</th>
        <th class="py-2 px-2 text-right">confirmed</th>
        <th class="py-2 px-2 text-right">password_created</th>
        <th class="py-2 pl-2 text-right">completion</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @weekly.each do |week, counts| %>
        <% started = counts['started'] || 0 %>
        <% created = counts['password_created'] || 0 %>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
          <td class="py-2 pr-2 font-mono"><%= week.strftime('%Y-%m-%d') %><%= ' *' if week == Date.current.beginning_of_week %></td>
          <td class="py-2 px-2 text-right tabular-nums"><%= started %></td>
          <td class="py-2 px-2 text-right tabular-nums"><%= counts['mail_sent'] || 0 %></td>
          <td class="py-2 px-2 text-right tabular-nums"><%= counts['mail_failed'] || 0 %></td>
          <td class="py-2 px-2 text-right tabular-nums"><%= (counts['confirmed_code'] || 0) + (counts['confirmed_magic_link'] || 0) %></td>
          <td class="py-2 px-2 text-right tabular-nums"><%= created %></td>
          <td class="py-2 pl-2 text-right tabular-nums font-bold"><%= started.positive? ? "#{(100.0 * created / started).round}%" : '–' %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p class="text-secondary text-sm">
    Weeks start on Monday; * marks the current, partial week. Completion is
    password_created / started within the same week, so a flow finished after
    a week boundary counts toward the later week.
  </p>

  <p class="text-secondary text-sm">
    Server-side Ahoy events, one per step — no e-mail or other personal
    data is recorded. Percentages are relative to <span class="font-mono">started</span>
    in the same window. Steps can exceed <span class="font-mono">started</span>
    when a flow resumes across windows or a mail is resent.
    Tracking live since 2026-08-12; bounce notices since 2026-10-22, counted once
    per bounced mail a person is shown (reloads don't count).
    <span class="font-mono">mail failed</span>: the mail never left — our SMTP
    provider refused it or could not be reached — by error, SMTP reply code and
    recipient kind (<span class="font-mono">microsoft</span> = hotmail/outlook/live/msn).
  </p>

  <h1 class="text-xl font-black text-center pt-12">
    Sign-in funnel
  </h1>

  <table class="w-full text-sm" id="sign_in">
    <thead>
      <tr class="border-b text-left">
        <th class="py-2 pr-2">Step</th>
        <% @windows.each_key do |label| %>
          <th class="py-2 px-2 text-right"><%= label %></th>
        <% end %>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% Root::FunnelController::SIGN_IN_STEPS.each do |step| %>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100 <%= 'font-bold' if step == 'signed_in' %>">
          <td class="py-2 pr-2 font-mono"><%= step %></td>
          <% @windows.each_key do |label| %>
            <% count = @sign_in_counts[label][step] || 0 %>
            <% started = @sign_in_counts[label]['started'] || 0 %>
            <td class="py-2 px-2 text-right tabular-nums">
              <%= count %>
              <% if step != 'started' && started.positive? %>
                <span class="text-secondary text-xs">(<%= (100.0 * count / started).round %>%)</span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
          <% end %>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
      <tr class="text-secondary">
        <td class="py-2 pr-2 font-mono">↳ handed_off by route</td>
        <% @windows.each_key do |label| %>
          <td class="py-2 px-2 text-right tabular-nums align-top text-xs">
            <% @handoffs[label].sort_by { |route, n| [-n, route] }.each do |route, n| %>
              <div><span class="font-mono"><%= route %></span> <%= n %></div>
            <% end %>
          </td>
        <% end %>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 class="font-bold pt-4">By week</h2>

  <table class="w-full text-sm" id="sign_in_weekly">
    <thead>
      <tr class="border-b text-left">
        <th class="py-2 pr-2">Week of</th>
        <% Root::FunnelController::SIGN_IN_STEPS.each do |step| %>
          <th class="py-2 px-2 text-right"><%= step %></th>
        <% end %>
        <th class="py-2 pl-2 text-right">completion</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <% @sign_in_weekly.each do |week, counts| %>
        <% started = counts['started'] || 0 %>
        <% signed_in = counts['signed_in'] || 0 %>
        <tr class="border-b border-gray-100">
          <td class="py-2 pr-2 font-mono"><%= week.strftime('%Y-%m-%d') %><%= ' *' if week == Date.current.beginning_of_week %></td>
          <% Root::FunnelController::SIGN_IN_STEPS.each do |step| %>
            <td class="py-2 px-2 text-right tabular-nums"><%= counts[step] || 0 %></td>
          <% end %>
          <td class="py-2 pl-2 text-right tabular-nums font-bold"><%= started.positive? ? "#{(100.0 * signed_in / started).round}%" : '–' %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <p class="text-secondary text-sm">
    <span class="font-mono">started</span>: a known e-mail was entered on the
    login page. <span class="font-mono">password_failed</span> counts every
    wrong attempt, so one person can add several.
    <span class="font-mono">signed_in</span>: the password was accepted;
    completion is signed_in / started. <span class="font-mono">handed_off</span>:
    an ID token went to a service — this includes the confirm page's button for
    people already signed in, so it can exceed signed_in. Its route is
    <span class="font-mono">password</span> (straight from the password form)
    or <span class="font-mono">confirm</span> (the confirm page's button), to an
    <span class="font-mono">app</span> (custom scheme) or the
    <span class="font-mono">web</span>; many confirm → app per person suggests
    an app that didn't open.
    Tracking live since this page's sign-in section was deployed.
  </p>

  <p class="text-center">
    <%= link_to '&larr; Relying parties'.html_safe, root_relying_parties_path %>
  </p>
</div>
